`,(0,d.jsx)(b3.p,{children:"I wanted to use a custom email address linked to this domain, and sought to find out how."}),`
`,(0,d.jsx)(b3.hr,{}),`
`,(0,d.jsx)(b3.h2,{children:"Why?"}),`
`,(0,d.jsx)(b3.p,{children:"I initally just went with Email Routing through Cloudflare after registering my domain with them. While it does a good job of email forwarding, I also wanted to be able to send emails from a custom address linked to my domain."}),`
`,(0,d.jsx)(b3.h2,{children:"How?"}),`
`,(0,d.jsxs)(b3.p,{children:["I found ",(0,d.jsx)(b3.a,{href:"https://migadu.com/",children:"Migadu"})," while going down a Reddit rabbit hole on SMTP providers. Initially I went with Brevo but seemingly it prevented me from setting up a simple account for supposed spam reasons, even though I never set an account with them before."]}),`
`,(0,d.jsxs)(b3.p,{children:["It involved setting up my domain with Migadu and manually entering the DNS records provided into Cloudflare. The records included TXT (unique verification of domain ownership to prevent hijacking), MX (",(0,d.jsx)(b3.a,{href:"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MX_record",children:"Mail exchanger"}),"), ",(0,d.jsx)(b3.a,{href:"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DomainKeys_Identified_Mail",children:"DomainKeys Identified Mail (DKIM)"})," for email auth through public cryptography, ",(0,d.jsx)(b3.a,{href:"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Authenticated_Received_Chain",children:"Authenticated Received Chain (ARC)"})," and ",(0,d.jsx)(b3.a,{href:"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sender_Policy_Framework",children:"SPF"}),". Optional were the ",(0,d.jsx)(b3.a,{href:"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DMARC",children:"DMARC"})," and Autoconfig/Autodiscovery. I manually entered these into Cloudflare's DNS records for my domain."]}),`
`,(0,d.jsxs)(b3.p,{children:["Afterwards, I followed the guide to configure Migadu with ",(0,d.jsx)(b3.a,{href:"https://migadu.com/guides/apple_mail/",children:"Apple Mail"}),". I had some difficulty with the ports here and wound up just automatically setting it with Mail, as manual port setting didn't work."]}),`
`,(0,d.jsx)(b3.p,{children:"Migadu then asked to confirm by running tests and now I'm able to send/receive emails with my custom domain! I also set up an alias to put on my CVs."}),`
`,(0,d.jsxs)(b3.ul,{children:[`
`,(0,d.jsxs)(b3.li,{children:[`
`,(0,d.jsxs)(b3.p,{children:[(0,d.jsx)(b3.strong,{children:"Learning Curve"}),": Not quite but manually having to enter each DNS record into Cloudflare, fine for one website but probably would be a hassle if I had multiple domains."]}),`
`]}),`
`,(0,d.jsxs)(b3.li,{children:[`
`,(0,d.jsxs)(b3.p,{children:[(0,d.jsx)(b3.strong,{children:"Challenges"}),": Some difficulty with setting up the DKIM record - I had to turn off the proxy in Cloudflare to successfully set it up."]}),`
`]}),`
`]}),`
